/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 56 0 R
/T (The client is an Indian custom-manufacturing business \(name withheld for confidentiality\) producing made-to-order furniture and upholstered goods for retail and hospitality customers. Production was coordinated through spreadsheets and disconnected trackers, making it difficult to see the live status of jobs, know exactly how much material was on hand versus already committed to a build, or generate an accurate invoice once a job was complete. As order volume grew, this manual approach led to double-booked materials, delayed billing, and limited visibility for managers tracking work across cutting, sewing, upholstery, and quality-check stages.)
/E (The client is an Indian custom-manufacturing business \(name withheld for confidentiality\) producing made-to-order furniture and upholstered goods for retail and hospitality customers. Production was coordinated through spreadsheets and disconnected trackers, making it difficult to see the live status of jobs, know exactly how much material was on hand versus already committed to a build, or generate an accurate invoice once a job was complete. As order volume grew, this manual approach led to double-booked materials, delayed billing, and limited visibility for managers tracking work across cutting, sewing, upholstery, and quality-check stages.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
